{"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Using-SwiftUsd-from-C++","generated":true,"title":"Using SwiftUsd from C++","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/SwiftCxxInteropMemorySafety","doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/SwiftCxxMacros"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/GettingStartedInCPlusPlus","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Getting Started","anchor":"Getting-Started","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Before you can start using SwiftUsd, you need to add it as a dependency to your Xcode project or Swift Package, and then configure a few build settings.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Despite the fact that SwiftUsd is a Swift Package, you can use it in a pure-C++ Xcode project\/target, as well as in a pure-C++ Swift Package target."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Package targets cannot mix Swift and C++ code in a single target. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-package-manager\/issues\/8945"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To do so, follow the steps in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/GettingStarted#Getting-Started","type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Getting Started for Swift","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Getting Started for Swift"}],"isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". If you’re using a pure-C++ target, you don’t need to change the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C++ and Objective-C Interoperability"},{"type":"text","text":" mode in Xcode or add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".interoperabilityMode(.Cxx)"},{"type":"text","text":" to your target’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftSettings"},{"type":"text","text":" in your Swift Package manifest."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Using SwiftUsd","anchor":"Using-SwiftUsd","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you’ve added SwiftUsd as a package dependency to your Xcode project or Swift package and set the C++ version to GNU++17, you’re ready to start using SwiftUsd:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#include <iostream>","#include \"pxr\/usd\/usd\/stage.h\"","#include \"pxr\/usd\/usd\/prim.h\"","#include \"pxr\/usd\/usdGeom\/tokens.h\"","","std::string makeHelloWorldString() {","    pxr::UsdStageRefPtr stage = pxr::UsdStage::CreateInMemory();","    stage->DefinePrim(pxr::SdfPath(\"\/hello\"), pxr::UsdGeomTokens->Cube);","    stage->DefinePrim(pxr::SdfPath(\"\/hello\/world\"), pxr::UsdGeomTokens->Sphere);","    std::string result;","    stage->ExportToString(&result);","    return result;","}","","int main(int argc, const char * argv[]) {","    std::cout << makeHelloWorldString() << std::endl;","    return 0;","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"c++"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To use new functions or types added by SwiftUsd, include the SwiftUsd umbrella header:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#include \"swiftUsd\/swiftUsd.h\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"c++"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This header lets you use macros useful for Swift-Cxx interop, functions that are important for memory safety with Swift-Cxx interop, and Swift wrapper types for C++ types not imported by Swift-Cxx interop."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Don’t include other files in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OpenUSD\/swiftUsd"},{"type":"text","text":", as they are implementation details and may change without warning"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/document